# /etc/paperbot/executor-gate.env  (root:root, chmod 600; made by install.sh from this template, filled by an owner)
# The keys of the friend's Gate account (owners 10-31, docs/gate-bot-ko.md: the 게이트 봇, paperbot-gateguard). systemd
# reads this file for that one unit only, so the other bots and this one never see each other's keys. Never commit the
# real file, never paste a key in a chat: write it on the server with
#   sudoedit /etc/paperbot/executor-gate.env
#
# Only the lines below: the bot refuses to start when another exchange's key (BYBIT_*, MEXC_*, WOOXPRO_*, TOOBIT_* ...)
# is in its environment.
#
# Gate: an APIv4 key made in the account (API 관리) with the perpetual futures permission (read and write) only, NO
# withdrawal, no spot / margin / wallet, bound to this server's IP 158.247.200.152; the key and the secret (shown once).
GATE_LIVE_KEY=
GATE_LIVE_SECRET=
# After checking the key page (futures only, no withdrawal, IP bound), write exactly FUTURES_ONLY_NO_WITHDRAW_IP_BOUND
# here (the bot refuses to start without it)
GATE_LIVE_KEY_CHECKED=
# The mainnet switch: exactly I_UNDERSTAND (the bot only trades for real: "mode": "mainnet" in gateguard.json).
PAPERBOT_LIVE_MAINNET=
# Alerts: /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env (the live bot's own token and the owners' private chats), loaded after this
# file by the unit, sets them; nothing to write here when that file has them. Without that file, remove the "#" and
# write the token and the chat ids (never leave a chat line empty: keep it commented out instead).
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO=
